speechtext:
It seems to me that the discussion has altogether changed since the last time we were considering this bill. I am sorry I was not in when the Minister of Fisheries was discussing the matter. What we objected to when the bill was previously under consideration was that the fishermen on the east and west coasts were excluded'from the insurance that was given
War Risk Insurance

to shipowners on inland waters and on rivers. I have the section before me. Section 2, paragraph (i) says:
"property" means buildings, machinery, fixtures or other structures erected or placed upon, in, over, under or affixed to land, and all movable corporeal property in Canada, but shall not include:
(i)	land, exclusive of any structures aforesaid;
(ii)	growing crops, plants and trees;
And then:
(iv) ships, other than vessels used solely in docks, ports, rivers or other inland waters or inland waterways;
I understand the suggestion was that fishing boats be included in the bill. I did not hear anything the last time about free insurance for fishing boats, and I cannot understand how it has come in. If the fishing fleet can get marine insurance at reasonable rates, I do not think we are on sound ground in asking that they be given free insurance under this bill, because no other commercial property receives free insurance.
